This problem can be solved in both ways 
Brute force appproach will be --> using 2 nested loops 
Optimal approach can be --> using 2 pointers

#Pattern found:
Area = width × height
     where
     width = right - left
     height = min(height[left], height[right])
   update max_area
   move pointers


Brute Force Approach:
----------------------------
n = list(map(int, input().split()))
max_area = 0
for i in range(len(n)):
    for j in range(i + 1, len(n)):
        width = j - i
        height = min(n[i], n[j])
        area = width * height
        if area > max_area:
            max_area = area
print(max_area)

TC:O(n²)
SC:O(1)


Optimal Approach:
----------------------------
n = list(map(int, input().split()))
left = 0
right = len(n) - 1
max_area = 0
while left < right:
    width = right - left
    height = min(n[left], n[right])
    area = width * height
    if area > max_area:
        max_area = area
    if n[left] < n[right]:
        left += 1
    else:
        right -= 1
print(max_area)

TC:O(n)
SC:O(1)
